// Generated by tools/build_site.py from content/free-questions — free practice questions.
(window.FREE_Q = window.FREE_Q || {})["mat"] = {"qs": [["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "Select the word that completes the analogy.\nOrnithology : Birds :: Entomology : ?", ["Fossils", "Words", "Insects", "Fungi"], 2, "Ornithology is the study of birds; entomology is the study of insects. Words are studied in etymology, fungi in mycology and fossils in palaeontology."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "The question is followed by two statements. Decide whether the data in the statements are sufficient to answer it.\n\nIs the integer n divisible by 6?\nI. n is divisible by 12.\nII. n is divisible by both 2 and 3.", ["Statement I alone is sufficient, but Statement II alone is not", "Both statements together are needed, but neither alone is sufficient", "Each statement alone is sufficient", "Statement II alone is sufficient, but Statement I alone is not"], 2, "Any multiple of 12 is a multiple of 6, so I answers 'yes'. Divisibility by both 2 and 3 (coprime) also means divisibility by 6. Each statement alone suffices."], ["Mathematical Skills", "In what ratio must rice costing ₹40 per kg be mixed with rice costing ₹55 per kg to get a mixture worth ₹45 per kg?", ["3 : 2", "1 : 2", "3 : 1", "2 : 1"], 3, "By alligation, cheaper : dearer = (55 − 45) : (45 − 40) = 10 : 5 = 2 : 1. Check: (2 × 40 + 1 × 55)/3 = 135/3 = ₹45."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "Students enrolled in four courses at an institute:\nCourse | 2022 | 2023 | 2024\nBBA | 400 | 460 | 520\nBCom | 600 | 570 | 630\nBSc | 350 | 420 | 490\nBA | 250 | 260 | 240\n\nBy what percentage did the total enrolment rise from 2022 to 2024?", ["15%", "16.4%", "18.2%", "17.5%"], 3, "Total 2022 = 400 + 600 + 350 + 250 = 1,600. Total 2024 = 520 + 630 + 490 + 240 = 1,880. Rise = 280/1,600 × 100 = 17.5%."], ["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "Find the next letter of the series.\nA, C, F, J, O, ?", ["V", "U", "T", "S"], 1, "The gaps increase by one each time: +2, +3, +4, +5. The next gap is +6, and O (15) + 6 = U (21)."], ["Mathematical Skills", "A's income is 20% less than B's. By what percentage is B's income more than A's?", ["22.5%", "20%", "24%", "25%"], 3, "If B = 100, A = 80. B exceeds A by 20 on a base of 80, i.e. 20/80 × 100 = 25%. The base changes, so the answer is not 20%."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "Annual profit (₹ lakh) of a firm: 2020 – 35, 2021 – 42, 2022 – 38, 2023 – 50, 2024 – 60.\n\nBy what percentage was the 2024 profit higher than the average annual profit for 2020–2024?", ["30%", "40%", "33.3%", "25%"], 2, "Average = (35 + 42 + 38 + 50 + 60)/5 = 225/5 = ₹45 lakh. 2024 profit of ₹60 lakh is 15/45 × 100 ≈ 33.3% higher."], ["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "Find the next term of the series.\n3, 8, 15, 24, 35, ?", ["46", "50", "48", "49"], 2, "The terms are n² − 1 for n = 2, 3, 4, 5, 6: 3, 8, 15, 24, 35. The next is 7² − 1 = 48. Equivalently, the differences 5, 7, 9, 11 continue with 13."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "A company's annual budget of ₹45 crore is allocated as: Production 40%, Salaries 20%, Marketing 18%, R&D 12%, Administration 10%.\n\nBy how much does the Marketing allocation exceed the Administration allocation?", ["₹3.2 crore", "₹8 crore", "₹4.5 crore", "₹3.6 crore"], 3, "Marketing − Administration = 18% − 10% = 8% of ₹45 crore = ₹3.6 crore. ₹8 crore mistakes the percentage gap for a rupee amount."], ["Mathematical Skills", "Three ropes of 84 m, 126 m and 210 m are to be cut into pieces of equal length, as long as possible, with nothing left over. How many pieces will there be in all?", ["14", "10", "8", "12"], 1, "The greatest common length is HCF(84, 126, 210) = 42 m. Pieces = 84/42 + 126/42 + 210/42 = 2 + 3 + 5 = 10."], ["Mathematical Skills", "Two trains 150 m and 100 m long run on parallel tracks in opposite directions at 54 km/h and 36 km/h. How long will they take to cross each other completely?", ["25 seconds", "9 seconds", "10 seconds", "12.5 seconds"], 2, "Relative speed = 54 + 36 = 90 km/h = 25 m/s. Distance = 150 + 100 = 250 m. Time = 250/25 = 10 seconds. Using the difference of speeds would wrongly give 25 seconds."], ["Mathematical Skills", "If α and β are the roots of x² − 7x + 12 = 0, what is the value of α² + β²?", ["49", "24", "25", "37"], 2, "α + β = 7 and αβ = 12. So α² + β² = (α + β)² − 2αβ = 49 − 24 = 25. The roots 3 and 4 confirm: 9 + 16 = 25."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "Students enrolled in four courses at an institute:\nCourse | 2022 | 2023 | 2024\nBBA | 400 | 460 | 520\nBCom | 600 | 570 | 630\nBSc | 350 | 420 | 490\nBA | 250 | 260 | 240\n\nBSc enrolment in 2024 was what percentage of BBA enrolment in 2022?", ["122.5%", "130%", "112.5%", "118.4%"], 0, "BSc 2024 = 490 and BBA 2022 = 400. 490/400 × 100 = 122.5%. Take care to compare the right course and the right year."], ["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "Five friends A, B, C, D and E sit in a row facing north.\n• B sits second to the left of D.\n• E sits immediately to the right of B.\n• A sits at one of the ends, to the left of C.\n• C is not next to A.\nWho sits in the middle?", ["C", "B", "D", "E"], 3, "A must be at the left end. B, E, D occupy three consecutive seats (B, E, then D), and C cannot be next to A, so the order is A, B, E, D, C. E is in the middle."], ["Language Comprehension", "Read the passage and answer the question.\n\nStepwells, found mainly in Gujarat and Rajasthan, were built to reach groundwater that sank far below the surface in the dry months. Flights of steps led down several storeys to the water, so that people could draw it whatever its level. Because the lower levels stayed cooler than the scorching ground above, stepwells also served as places of rest and social gathering, and many were richly carved. Under colonial rule, piped water and hand-pumps were promoted as more hygienic, and many stepwells fell into neglect, some becoming dumps for rubbish. Today a number are being restored, not only as heritage sites but also as a way of recharging groundwater in regions where it is being rapidly depleted.\n\nWhich of the following is NOT mentioned in the passage as a role of stepwells?", ["Providing access to groundwater", "Serving as a place for social gathering", "Offering a cool place to rest", "Storing grain during famines"], 3, "The passage mentions access to groundwater, cool lower levels for rest, and social gathering. Storage of grain is never mentioned, so it is the answer."], ["Language Comprehension", "Read the passage and answer the question.\n\nStepwells, found mainly in Gujarat and Rajasthan, were built to reach groundwater that sank far below the surface in the dry months. Flights of steps led down several storeys to the water, so that people could draw it whatever its level. Because the lower levels stayed cooler than the scorching ground above, stepwells also served as places of rest and social gathering, and many were richly carved. Under colonial rule, piped water and hand-pumps were promoted as more hygienic, and many stepwells fell into neglect, some becoming dumps for rubbish. Today a number are being restored, not only as heritage sites but also as a way of recharging groundwater in regions where it is being rapidly depleted.\n\nAs used in the passage, the word 'depleted' most nearly means:", ["used up", "measured", "polluted", "replenished"], 0, "Depleted means reduced or exhausted. Restoring stepwells to recharge groundwater makes sense only if groundwater is being used up. 'Replenished' is the opposite, and 'polluted' changes quality, not quantity."], ["Language Comprehension", "Ravi is frugal: he cooks at home and saves most of his salary. Pick the antonym of 'frugal'.", ["Economical", "Extravagant", "Prudent", "Thrifty"], 1, "Frugal means careful and sparing with money. Extravagant, meaning spending lavishly, is its opposite. Thrifty and economical are synonyms, and prudent is close in sense."], ["Mathematical Skills", "A card is drawn at random from a well-shuffled pack of 52 cards. What is the probability that it is a king or a heart?", ["4/13", "1/4", "5/13", "17/52"], 0, "Kings: 4, hearts: 13, king of hearts counted twice: 1. Favourable = 4 + 13 − 1 = 16, so probability = 16/52 = 4/13. Not subtracting the overlap gives 17/52."], ["Mathematical Skills", "Five years ago, the ratio of the ages of A and B was 3 : 4. Five years from now, it will be 5 : 6. What is A's present age?", ["30 years", "25 years", "15 years", "20 years"], 3, "Let ages five years ago be 3k and 4k. Then (3k + 10)/(4k + 10) = 5/6, so 18k + 60 = 20k + 50 and k = 5. A is 15 + 5 = 20 years now."], ["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "Ravi walks 5 km south, turns left and walks 3 km, then turns left again and walks 9 km. How far and in which direction is he now from his starting point?", ["7 km, North-East", "5 km, North-West", "4 km, North", "5 km, North-East"], 3, "Facing south, a left turn means east (3 km); another left means north (9 km). Net position: 3 km east and 4 km north, so he is √(9 + 16) = 5 km away towards the north-east."], ["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "Statement: Several cases of food poisoning were reported after a wedding feast in a town.\nCourses of action:\nI. The health department should collect samples of the food served and investigate.\nII. All weddings in the town should be banned for a year.\nWhich course of action follows?", ["Neither I nor II follows", "Only I follows", "Both I and II follow", "Only II follows"], 1, "Investigating the food is a practical step to find the cause and prevent repetition. Banning all weddings is an extreme reaction that does not address the actual problem, so only I follows."], ["Language Comprehension", "Fill in the blank with the correct preposition.\nShe has been working in this company ______ 2019.", ["for", "from", "by", "since"], 3, "With the present perfect continuous, 'since' is used before a point in time (2019) and 'for' before a period (five years). 'From' needs an end point such as 'to 2023'."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "A company's annual budget of ₹45 crore is allocated as: Production 40%, Salaries 20%, Marketing 18%, R&D 12%, Administration 10%.\n\nWhat central angle would represent R&D in a pie chart of this budget?", ["36°", "43.2°", "48.6°", "40.8°"], 1, "Central angle = share × 360°. R&D = 12% of 360° = 43.2°. 36° corresponds to Administration's 10%."], ["Language Comprehension", "Read the passage and answer the question.\n\nStepwells, found mainly in Gujarat and Rajasthan, were built to reach groundwater that sank far below the surface in the dry months. Flights of steps led down several storeys to the water, so that people could draw it whatever its level. Because the lower levels stayed cooler than the scorching ground above, stepwells also served as places of rest and social gathering, and many were richly carved. Under colonial rule, piped water and hand-pumps were promoted as more hygienic, and many stepwells fell into neglect, some becoming dumps for rubbish. Today a number are being restored, not only as heritage sites but also as a way of recharging groundwater in regions where it is being rapidly depleted.\n\nAccording to the passage, stepwells had long flights of steps mainly:", ["to give access to water whose level changed through the year", "to display the wealth of their builders", "to keep animals away from the water", "to provide seating for large public ceremonies held at the well"], 0, "The passage says steps led down several storeys 'so that people could draw it whatever its level', because groundwater sank in the dry months. The other purposes are not stated."], ["Language Comprehension", "Choose the correct meaning of the idiom 'a red herring'.", ["An embarrassing mistake made in public", "A rare and valuable opportunity that should be seized", "A warning sign of danger ahead", "Something that distracts attention from the real issue"], 3, "A red herring is a misleading clue or irrelevant point that draws attention away from the main question, common in debates and detective stories. It has nothing to do with danger signs or opportunities."], ["Language Comprehension", "Fill in the blank with the most appropriate word.\nThe committee's report was so ______ that even experts struggled to follow its argument.", ["concise", "lucid", "convoluted", "candid"], 2, "'Even experts struggled to follow' signals a report that was complicated and hard to follow, which is convoluted. Lucid and concise would make it easy to follow; candid concerns honesty, not clarity."], ["Mathematical Skills", "An article marked at ₹1,200 is sold at a 15% discount and the seller still makes a 20% profit. What is its cost price?", ["₹900", "₹816", "₹850", "₹880"], 2, "Selling price = 85% of 1,200 = ₹1,020. Since this includes 20% profit, cost price = 1,020/1.2 = ₹850. Taking 20% off 1,020 wrongly gives ₹816."], ["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "Pointing to a man, Meera said, \"His father is the only son of my father's father.\" How is the man related to Meera?", ["Uncle", "Cousin", "Brother", "Nephew"], 2, "The only son of Meera's paternal grandfather is Meera's own father. So the man's father is Meera's father, which makes the man her brother."], ["Mathematical Skills", "What is the difference between compound interest and simple interest on ₹12,000 for 2 years at 10% per annum (compounded annually)?", ["₹120", "₹132", "₹240", "₹100"], 0, "For 2 years, CI − SI = P(r/100)² = 12,000 × 0.01 = ₹120. CI = ₹2,520 and SI = ₹2,400, confirming the difference."], ["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "Statement: The city council has decided to plant 10,000 saplings along highways to reduce air pollution.\nAssumptions:\nI. Trees can help reduce air pollution.\nII. Air pollution in the city is caused only by vehicles on highways.\nWhich assumption is implicit?", ["Only assumption II is implicit", "Neither I nor II is implicit", "Only assumption I is implicit", "Both I and II are implicit"], 2, "The decision makes sense only if trees help reduce pollution, so I is implicit. The council need not believe highways are the only source; planting along them can help even if other sources exist."], ["Language Comprehension", "Choose the one word for: 'a person who can speak several languages'.", ["Polymath", "Ventriloquist", "Polyglot", "Bibliophile"], 2, "A polyglot knows or speaks many languages. A polymath has wide learning in many subjects, a bibliophile loves books, and a ventriloquist throws his voice."], ["Language Comprehension", "Identify the part of the sentence that contains an error.\nHe is one of those leaders / who has always / put the country / before himself.", ["who has always", "He is one of those leaders", "before himself", "put the country"], 0, "In 'one of those leaders who…', the relative pronoun 'who' refers to the plural 'leaders', so the verb must be plural: 'who have always put the country before themselves'."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "In a survey of 500 people, 300 were men and 200 were women. 180 of the men and 90 of the women preferred tea; everyone else preferred coffee.\n\nWhat percentage of the people who preferred coffee were women?", ["55%", "52.2%", "45%", "47.8%"], 3, "Coffee: men 300 − 180 = 120, women 200 − 90 = 110, total 230. Women's share = 110/230 × 100 ≈ 47.8%. 55% is the share of women who prefer coffee, a different base."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "The question is followed by two statements. Decide whether the data in the statements are sufficient to answer it.\n\nWhat is the cost price of an article?\nI. It was sold for ₹550 at a profit of 10%.\nII. It was marked at ₹700 and sold at a discount of ₹150.", ["Statement II alone is sufficient, but Statement I alone is not", "Statement I alone is sufficient, but Statement II alone is not", "Each statement alone is sufficient", "Both statements together are needed, but neither alone is sufficient"], 1, "I gives cost price = 550/1.1 = ₹500. II gives only the selling price (₹550) with no profit information, so it cannot give the cost price."], ["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "In a certain code, LAMP is written as OZNK. How will GOLD be written in that code?", ["TLOW", "TMOW", "TLOX", "SLOW"], 0, "Each letter is replaced by its mirror letter in the alphabet (A↔Z, B↔Y, and so on; positions add up to 27). G→T, O→L, L→O, D→W, giving TLOW."], ["Language Comprehension", "Identify the part of the sentence that contains an error.\nNeither the manager nor his assistants / was present / at the meeting / held yesterday.", ["held yesterday", "was present", "at the meeting", "Neither the manager nor his assistants"], 1, "With 'neither…nor', the verb agrees with the nearer subject. 'Assistants' is plural, so the verb should be 'were present', not 'was present'."], ["Mathematical Skills", "A right circular cone has base radius 7 cm and slant height 25 cm. What is its volume? (Take π = 22/7)", ["1,320 cm³", "1,232 cm³", "3,696 cm³", "1,540 cm³"], 1, "Height = √(25² − 7²) = 24 cm. Volume = (1/3) × (22/7) × 49 × 24 = 1,232 cm³. Forgetting the 1/3 gives 3,696 cm³."], ["Mathematical Skills", "The average of 11 numbers is 50. The average of the first six is 49 and that of the last six is 52. What is the sixth number?", ["51", "56", "54", "60"], 1, "The sixth number is counted in both groups: 6 × 49 + 6 × 52 − 11 × 50 = 294 + 312 − 550 = 56."], ["Mathematical Skills", "In how many different ways can the letters of the word MANAGER be arranged?", ["5,040", "1,260", "720", "2,520"], 3, "MANAGER has 7 letters with A repeated twice and the rest distinct. Arrangements = 7!/2! = 5,040/2 = 2,520."], ["Language Comprehension", "A meticulous editor checks every comma twice. Which word is a synonym of 'meticulous' here?", ["Painstaking", "Careless", "Indifferent", "Hasty"], 0, "Meticulous means showing great attention to detail, which is what painstaking means. Careless and hasty are nearly opposite, and indifferent means lacking interest."], ["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "If 15 August 2026 falls on a Saturday, on which day will 15 August 2027 fall?", ["Monday", "Saturday", "Sunday", "Friday"], 2, "The period from 15 August 2026 to 15 August 2027 contains February 2027, which is not a leap month, so there are 365 days, or 1 odd day. Saturday + 1 = Sunday."], ["Language Comprehension", "Which of the following words is spelt correctly?", ["Millenium", "Occurence", "Embarassment", "Accommodate"], 3, "Accommodate has double 'c' and double 'm'. The correct spellings of the others are occurrence (double r), embarrassment (double r and double s) and millennium (double l and double n)."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "The question is followed by two statements. Decide whether the data in the statements are sufficient to answer it.\n\nWho is the tallest among P, Q and R?\nI. P is taller than Q but shorter than R.\nII. R is taller than Q.", ["Both statements together are needed, but neither alone is sufficient", "Statement II alone is sufficient, but Statement I alone is not", "Each statement alone is sufficient", "Statement I alone is sufficient, but Statement II alone is not"], 3, "I gives the full order R > P > Q, so R is tallest. II says nothing about P, who could be taller or shorter than R."], ["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "Select the letter group that does NOT belong with the others.", ["RTW", "BDF", "HJL", "MOQ"], 0, "In BDF, HJL and MOQ, each letter is two places after the previous one. In RTW the gaps are two and then three (R→T→W), so it is the odd one out."], ["Mathematical Skills", "What is the smallest number that leaves a remainder of 4 when divided by 6, 8 or 12, and is exactly divisible by 11?", ["220", "172", "244", "196"], 0, "Such numbers have the form 24k + 4 (LCM of 6, 8, 12 is 24). Testing k = 1, 2, 3, …, the first divisible by 11 is k = 9: 24 × 9 + 4 = 220 = 11 × 20."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "The question is followed by two statements. Decide whether the data in the statements are sufficient to answer it.\n\nHow many days will B alone take to finish a piece of work?\nI. A and B together finish it in 6 days.\nII. A alone finishes it in 10 days.", ["Both statements together are needed, but neither alone is sufficient", "Statement I alone is sufficient, but Statement II alone is not", "Each statement alone is sufficient", "Statement II alone is sufficient, but Statement I alone is not"], 0, "Neither statement alone gives B's rate. Together, B's rate = 1/6 − 1/10 = 1/15, so B takes 15 days. Both are needed."], ["Mathematical Skills", "Walking at three-fourths of his usual speed, a man reaches his office 20 minutes late. What is his usual time for the journey?", ["45 minutes", "80 minutes", "60 minutes", "40 minutes"], 2, "At 3/4 of the speed, time becomes 4/3 of usual. Extra time = (4/3 − 1) × t = t/3 = 20 minutes, so t = 60 minutes."], ["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "What is the angle between the hour and minute hands of a clock at 3:40?", ["110°", "130°", "120°", "140°"], 1, "Angle = |30H − 5.5M| = |30 × 3 − 5.5 × 40| = |90 − 220| = 130°. Ignoring the hour hand's movement past 3 would wrongly give 120°."], ["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "In a row of 40 students, Ravi is 14th from the left end. Kiran is 9th to the right of Ravi. What is Kiran's position from the right end?", ["17th", "18th", "19th", "23rd"], 1, "Kiran is 14 + 9 = 23rd from the left. Position from the right = 40 − 23 + 1 = 18th. 23rd is his position from the left, a common trap."], ["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "Statements:\nNo doctor is a lawyer.\nSome lawyers are writers.\nConclusions:\nI. Some writers are not doctors.\nII. Some doctors are writers.", ["Both conclusions follow", "Neither conclusion follows", "Only conclusion II follows", "Only conclusion I follows"], 3, "The writers who are lawyers cannot be doctors, since no doctor is a lawyer, so some writers are certainly not doctors. Nothing links doctors to writers directly, so II is only a possibility."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "The question is followed by two statements. Decide whether the data in the statements are sufficient to answer it.\n\nWhat is the value of the integer x?\nI. x² = 16\nII. x > 0", ["Statement II alone is sufficient, but Statement I alone is not", "Statement I alone is sufficient, but Statement II alone is not", "Both statements together are needed, but neither alone is sufficient", "Each statement alone is sufficient"], 2, "I alone gives x = 4 or −4, and II alone gives any positive integer. Together they fix x = 4, so both are needed."], ["Language Comprehension", "Read the passage and answer the question.\n\nStepwells, found mainly in Gujarat and Rajasthan, were built to reach groundwater that sank far below the surface in the dry months. Flights of steps led down several storeys to the water, so that people could draw it whatever its level. Because the lower levels stayed cooler than the scorching ground above, stepwells also served as places of rest and social gathering, and many were richly carved. Under colonial rule, piped water and hand-pumps were promoted as more hygienic, and many stepwells fell into neglect, some becoming dumps for rubbish. Today a number are being restored, not only as heritage sites but also as a way of recharging groundwater in regions where it is being rapidly depleted.\n\nWhich of the following can be inferred from the passage?", ["Piped water reached the stepwell regions only after independence.", "Stepwells may have practical value beyond their historical importance.", "All the stepwells in Rajasthan have now been fully restored.", "Stepwells were built mainly to store rainwater for temples."], 1, "Restoration is valued 'not only as heritage sites but also' for recharging groundwater, which shows a practical value. The passage says only 'a number' are being restored and links piped water to colonial rule."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "The question is followed by two statements. Decide whether the data in the statements are sufficient to answer it.\n\nWhat is the speed of a boat in still water?\nI. The speed of the stream is 2 km/h.\nII. The boat goes 24 km downstream in 2 hours and returns upstream in 3 hours.", ["Statement I alone is sufficient, but Statement II alone is not", "Statement II alone is sufficient, but Statement I alone is not", "Both statements together are needed, but neither alone is sufficient", "Each statement alone is sufficient"], 1, "II gives downstream speed 12 km/h and upstream 8 km/h, so still-water speed = (12 + 8)/2 = 10 km/h. I alone gives only the stream's speed."], ["Language Comprehension", "The first sentence is given. Arrange P, Q, R and S to form a coherent paragraph.\n1. The monsoon is vital to Indian agriculture.\nP. As a result, a delayed or weak monsoon can hurt farm output and rural incomes.\nQ. A large part of the country's farmland depends on rainfall rather than irrigation.\nR. This, in turn, can push up food prices in towns and cities.\nS. Policymakers therefore track the monsoon's progress closely.", ["PQRS", "QPRS", "QPSR", "QRPS"], 1, "Q explains why the monsoon is vital; P gives the result ('As a result'); R extends the effect to cities ('in turn'); S concludes ('therefore'). Hence QPRS."], ["Intelligence & Critical Reasoning", "A shop moved its umbrellas next to the entrance, and umbrella sales over the following month rose by 40%. The manager concluded that the new placement caused the rise. Which of the following, if true, most weakens this conclusion?", ["The month after the move had unusually heavy and frequent rain.", "The shop also sells raincoats, which were kept in their original place.", "Umbrellas at the shop are priced slightly below those of nearby stores.", "Customers notice items placed near the entrance more often than others."], 0, "Heavy rain offers an alternative cause for higher umbrella sales, weakening the claim that placement was responsible. The point about customers noticing entrance items would actually support the manager's conclusion."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "Students enrolled in four courses at an institute:\nCourse | 2022 | 2023 | 2024\nBBA | 400 | 460 | 520\nBCom | 600 | 570 | 630\nBSc | 350 | 420 | 490\nBA | 250 | 260 | 240\n\nIn how many courses was the 2024 enrolment more than 20% higher than the 2022 enrolment?", ["3", "2", "1", "4"], 1, "BBA rose 30% (400 to 520) and BSc 40% (350 to 490). BCom rose only 5% and BA fell 4%. So two courses qualify."], ["Language Comprehension", "Choose the correct indirect speech of: He said, \"I will finish the report tomorrow.\"", ["He told that he would finish the report the next day.", "He said that I would finish the report the next day.", "He said that he would finish the report the next day.", "He said that he will finish the report tomorrow."], 2, "In reported speech after a past reporting verb, 'will' becomes 'would', 'I' becomes 'he' and 'tomorrow' becomes 'the next day'. 'Told' needs an object, so 'He told that' is incorrect."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "Annual profit (₹ lakh) of a firm: 2020 – 35, 2021 – 42, 2022 – 38, 2023 – 50, 2024 – 60.\n\nIn which year was the percentage increase in profit over the previous year the highest?", ["2023", "2024", "2022", "2021"], 0, "Changes: 2021 +20%, 2022 −9.5%, 2023 +31.6% (38 to 50), 2024 +20%. 2024 has the largest absolute rise (10), but 2023 has the highest percentage rise."], ["Mathematical Skills", "A starts a business with ₹30,000. After 4 months, B joins with ₹40,000. Out of a profit of ₹17,000 at the end of the year, what is B's share?", ["₹8,000", "₹9,000", "₹7,500", "₹8,500"], 0, "Capital × time: A = 30,000 × 12 = 3,60,000; B = 40,000 × 8 = 3,20,000. Ratio 9 : 8, so B gets 8/17 × 17,000 = ₹8,000."], ["Data Analysis & Sufficiency", "In a survey of 500 people, 300 were men and 200 were women. 180 of the men and 90 of the women preferred tea; everyone else preferred coffee.\n\nWhat is the ratio of people who preferred tea to those who preferred coffee?", ["27 : 23", "23 : 27", "9 : 11", "3 : 2"], 0, "Tea = 180 + 90 = 270; coffee = 500 − 270 = 230. Ratio 270 : 230 = 27 : 23. Reversing the order gives 23 : 27."]]};
